# Mobile-responsive design

- Treat mobile responsiveness as required for all new and changed UI.
- Support narrow phone widths from 320px through tablet and desktop sizes without horizontal page overflow.
- Reflow navigation, grids, typography, forms, previews, and imagery to fit; keep essential navigation and controls available on touch screens.
- Use fluid sizing, responsive images, CSS Grid/Flexbox, and logical properties where possible.
- Preserve readable text, visible focus, keyboard access, and comfortable touch targets at every breakpoint.
- Check designs at representative phone, tablet, and desktop widths before considering a UI complete.
